[candidate · 11:25] Good — that 40% matches what I backed into, which gives me confidence the decomposition is right. Beans went from 10.5 to roughly 14.7 points of revenue, and everything else moved at a similar rate. So it's broad commodity and input inflation, not a single bad supplier contract.

Let me size the fix. To get back to 24% margin I need to recover 18 points. If I hold volume and raise prices by x, revenue becomes 1+x while costs stay flat at 94 points. Margin = (1+x − 0.94)/(1+x) = 0.24 implies 1+x = 0.94/0.76 = 1.24. So roughly a 24% price increase — that's a lot to ask of a customer in one move.

Two questions before I recommend. Do we know what competitors have done on price over the same period? And has anyone tested elasticity — what happened to traffic the last time prices moved?
